{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040025-learning-2e-rules","id":1040025,"title":"Learning 2e Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T09:08:03-08:00","id":1040025,"title":"Learning 2e Rules","content":"Hey ho.<br /> <br /> So I really love the 2e rules changes they've made. But I'm having trouble getting my head around all the rules changes. <br /> <br /> Is there any resources that folk would recommend (apart from the books) to help learn the rules set? Or at least a method to work through them? I'm the GM of our group, so it's more important for me to know this stuff in general.<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> C","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:21:38-08:00","id":1040030,"title":"","content":"Is there something in particular you're struggling with? I've found for the most part that the rules are fairly similar. The biggest differences are the new subsystems and Conditions and Tilts. The latter I've found easy to manage if you use physical cards, either hand-written on notecards, printed out, or if you want to be really fancy, bought from drivethruRPG. As for the subsystems, such as Social Maneuvering, Chases, Investigations, and Crafting Equipment, remember that they're all optional. If you're feeling overwhelmed, feel free not to use all of them. Introduce one or two that you like and just get used to using it before you bring any more subsystems in. Heck, those of us who started 2e with the God-Machine Chronicle has been running without Chases, Investigations, or Crafting Equipment for two years before the Chronicles of Darkness book came out and introduced them. I still don't use Investigations, though I'm going to try it for the first time in a one-shot I'm running on Tuesday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:22:37-08:00","id":1040032,"title":"","content":"Stick to one new mechanics part at the time. I would go with Aspirations, Beats and Conditions on start, as they are heart and soul of 2E games. If you run mortals games, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570636-what-integrity-mean\">topics to understand Integrity</a> will really help you also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:00:51-08:00","id":1040066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040025-learning-2e-rules?p=1040032#post1040032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stick to one new mechanics part at the time. I would go with Aspirations, Beats and Conditions on start, as they are heart and soul of 2E games. If you run mortals games, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570636-what-integrity-mean\">topics to understand Integrity</a> will really help you also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, wyrd is on point here: these are the fundamentals. Grasp these and you can move on to the other new subsystems that Charlaquin mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:50:07-08:00","id":1040119,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, that's ideal. <br /> <br /> You're right, the bits I was struggling most with was the aspirations, beats and conditions. <br /> <br /> I think I probably bit off more than I could chew, as I was trying to get my head around that, the new combat tweaks, and also trying to get in Social Maneuvering, Chases and Investigation. <br /> <br /> I'll go back to square one, start slow. Really really looking forward to getting stuck into VtR and the rest though. (And Geist 2e when the time comes!).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:29:14-08:00","id":1040136,"title":"","content":"If you're looking to run VtR, there's a 2e ST screen on Drivethru, which can be useful to be able to quickly reference rules. Or you could make your own by printing sections you expect you'll need to review and adhering them to a folding board.<br /> <br /> The core rules you'll want to be most familiar with are the combat tweaks and the Conditions and Beats system. You don't necessarily need to memorize all of the Conditions in the book. Buy, print, or make cards to keep track of them, and hand them to players so they know what the Conditions affecting their characters do. Encourage the players to take an active role in making their Conditions relevant in the story. I might even say don't sweat Aspirations until you've had a chace to play around with Conditions and get a feel for them. Maybe run some one-shot games, or if one-shots aren't your thing, try using flat XP per session instead of Beats at first. Either way, try giving Willpower instead of Beats for resolving Conditions, so you can get used to using them and your players can get used to the player-as-director-style thinking where they're engaging with the Conditions for a positive incentive, much like with Virtue and Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:22:45-08:00","id":1040274,"title":"","content":"On the subject of handouts does anyone know of anywhere with a quick to download or copy/past collection of the conditions? I'd like to print some out for my group but having access to my books and a printer at the same time isn't common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:50:53-08:00","id":1040418,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/122721/GodMachine-Condition-Cards?term=condition+ca&amp;test_epoch=0\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>. The PDF is two bucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:10:11-08:00","id":1041604,"title":"","content":"I'm having issues with the new book myself. I get that in-depth systems can be cool if used properly, but when I got to the mechanics section in Chronicles, I was a little put-off. My biggest problem is that I don't see alternate rules for the Investigations, Social Maneuvering, Chasing or Combat sections, so they don't really seem optional to me. Are there 'official' alternate rules for these in the book that I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","user":"E11even-E11even","date":". 01-31-2017, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:39:09-08:00","id":1041622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040025-learning-2e-rules?p=1041604#post1041604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having issues with the new book myself. I get that in-depth systems can be cool if used properly, but when I got to the mechanics section in Chronicles, I was a little put-off. My biggest problem is that I don't see alternate rules for the Investigations, Social Maneuvering, Chasing or Combat sections, so they don't really seem optional to me. Are there 'official' alternate rules for these in the book that I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;alternate rules&quot; for Investigations, Social Maneuvering, and Chasing are using ordinary Skill rolls with the normal dice mechanics. Combat's abbreviated system is Down And Dirty Combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:54:37-08:00","id":1041625,"title":"","content":"Ah, so just using normal skill rolls would be the replacement. Since I couldn't seem to find anywhere in the book that these are actually optional, I thought that maybe I was missing something. When something this complex isn't optional, I'm wary about replacing it because other rules could be balanced with it in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:44:00-08:00","id":1041644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040025-learning-2e-rules?p=1041625#post1041625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so just using normal skill rolls would be the replacement. Since I couldn't seem to find anywhere in the book that these are actually optional, I thought that maybe I was missing something. When something this complex isn't optional, I'm wary about replacing it because other rules could be balanced with it in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, strictly speaking, every mechanic and subsystem is optional if you don't like it, ChroD is all about the toolbox. Some systems just take more work to replace or ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:00:12-08:00","id":1041650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040025-learning-2e-rules?p=1041625#post1041625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so just using normal skill rolls would be the replacement. Since I couldn't seem to find anywhere in the book that these are actually optional, I thought that maybe I was missing something. When something this complex isn't optional, I'm wary about replacing it because other rules could be balanced with it in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my reply in your other thread. These rules aren't 'optional' (except from the view that every rule is optional), they just exist as frameworks for when your story's investigations, interpersonal interactions, or chases are more involved (and possibly dramatic) than 'make one roll, I'll work out what that means for the whole thing'.<br /> <br /> Give them a chance. They may seem complex on the surface, since they introduce new labels for things you've probably always done but never thought about, but they're not really that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:43:58-08:00","id":1041879,"title":"","content":"One thing that I have found that really helps with Social Maneuvering (and probably Investigations but I haven't ran that) is to NOT think of it as social combat. This means two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Doors are NOT social 'health', thinking of it that way just makes it into a number crunch which is not the intention.<br /> 2) A given Social Maneuvering attempt is not done in a single Scene (or all at athe same time at all) the way combat is. When you are targeting someone with rolls that are a day or more apart, don't do all the rolls back to back. Do one, then go about the rest of the story and come back to the Maneuvering when it makes sense.<br /> <br /> My players had a hard time with SM at first too, but that turned out to be that when they read it they interpreted it as a thing that we would stop and do for 20 minutes like combat. Once I explained that it was more of a overall framing device for using the standard Skill rolls in a structured way it clicked much better for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Added missing 'w' 02-01-2017, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}